            <ArticleTitle>Paraperitoneal inguinal hernia of ureter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3941/jrcr.v6i8.1027</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inguinal herniation of ureter is an uncommon finding that can potentially lead to obstructive uropathy. We report a case of inguinal herniation of ureter discovered incidentally during workup for acute renal failure and ultrasound finding of hydronephrosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
